About Us
ADW Johnson is a multi-disciplinary company specialising in Urban Design, Planning, Engineering, Project Management, Surveying and Landscape Architecture with offices in Newcastle, the Central Coast, and in Sydney. We are passionate about development and treat each and every project as if it is our own. We use our expertise, dedication and hard work to forge long-term relationships with our clients and deliver best development outcomes. 
About The Opportunity
We are now looking for a Trainee Draftsperson to join our company at our Central Coast office.
With the wide variety of land development, high end residential and infrastructure projects ADW Johnson is involved with, there will be an opportunity to work on diverse projects in a supportive and stimulating environment.
Successful candidates will undertake engineering studies at TAFE, typically one day a week, as part of a recognised traineeship. The remaining four days will be spent in the office where you will be provided on-the-job training and mentoring. In addition to a competitive salary, all TAFE fees for your studies will be reimbursed.
Reporting directly to the Drafting Coordinator some of your responsibilities will include:
·       Plan drafting and communicating with the supervisor in relation to job status; 
·       Liaising with your supervisor and other staff in relation to workload planning and drafting instructions;
·       Working effectively and collaboratively as part of a project team; and
·       Completing quality assurance checklists.
This role offers the following benefits:
·       An exciting opportunity to work with some of NSW's leading developers;
·       Variety of projects, including land development, high-end residential, and infrastructure, from planning through to construction completion;
·       Paid TAFE certification;
·       A tailored career development program for career advancement;
·       A steady stream of interesting projects;
·       A positive work environment with flexible hours and social activities;
·       Competitive salary based on skills and experience;
·       Access to a generous overtime system.
About You 
The ideal candidate will have recently completed their School Certificate or HSC, or begun a Drafting course at TAFE, with a keen interest in pursuing a drafting career. Desired skills include:
·       Excellent communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively in a team;
·       Enthusiasm and a passion for the construction and engineering industries;
·       Strong written and verbal communication abilities;
·       A strong work ethic and keen attention to detail.

Coffey Testing is currently seeking motivated Entry-Level Construction Materials Testing (CMT) Technicians to join us in our location based at Adelaide Laboratory.
Coffey Testing - A bit about us!
We are one of Australia’s largest construction materials testing providers. We have been delivering testing services to the transport infrastructure, oil and gas and mining industries for over 65 years. We have an extensive network of permanent and site-specific testing facilities located across Australia, including in some of Australia’s most remote locations.
With that amount of experience and millions of tests under our belt – our clients choose us to provide deep insights into the properties of the materials they’re dealing with. We apply specialised testing and analysis services, using international best practice and conformance standards to achieve detailed, quality results. We provide independent NATA accredited testing services.
The Opportunities
If you are someone who would like to play a vital role in ensuring the quality and safety of the construction materials used in some of Australia’s largest rail, mining and infrastructure projects, we want to hear from you! Our mission is "We work with the best, because only the best wants what Coffey Testing can provide...peace of mind". We are built on teamwork to ensure we deliver quality results, safely to our clients and recognise that without the hard work of our people, this would not be possible. 
What a Construction Materials Testing (CMT) Technician does
As a new starter, you'll work alongside experienced technicians learning how to test construction materials such as soil, concrete and aggregates. You'll spend time both in the laboratory and on construction sites, collecting samples, performing tests, recording results, and helping ensure projects are built to specification.
A typical day might involve:
- Travelling to project sites to carry out field testing.
- Sampling soils, aggregates, concrete, and other construction materials.
- Performing tests in line with relevant test methods, to a high level of quality and ensuring integrity of results
- Recording and reporting test results into Geotester.
- Working closely with site supervisors, engineers, and project teams.
- Learning industry standards and quality requirements. 
As your experience grows, so do the opportunities. Experienced technicians take on more responsibility including:
- Managing testing programs on major infrastructure projects.
- Operating independently across multiple sites.
- Supervising junior technicians.
- Leading site laboratories on large projects.
- Progressing into senior technical, laboratory management, project management, or leadership roles. 
What we look for in a candidate
We are built on teamwork to ensure we deliver quality results safely to our clients. We recognise that without the hard work of our people, this would not be possible. We’re seeking a candidate whose values reflect our own who is someone that demonstrates integrity, takes ownership and pride in their work, works collaboratively as part of a team, and is driven to continuously deliver high-quality results you are someone that aligns with our values and has the below qualities and meets the criteria, we encourage you to apply:
- You are safety conscious and practice this everyday;
- You have pride in your work and expect quality outcomes from yourself;
- You are motivated and willing to learn;
- You can be trusted to work autonomously and enjoy working as part of a team;
- You are physically fit and are capable of repeatedly lifting loads of 15kg and over;
- You work well under pressure and can prioritise your workload to meet client demands;
- You are comfortable using computer software technology;
- You hold a current manual driver's licence (advantageous). 
What Coffey Testing Offers
To help you get to know us, all successful candidates attend our Training Academy in their first week. The program provides a thorough introduction to our company history, policies, processes, and procedures, along with practical, on-the-job training in our laboratory where you will learn a range of testing methods. We also offer structured career progression, supporting your development from entry-level CMT Technician (T1/T2) to advanced Technician roles (T3/T4) as your skills and experience grow
We believe that our employees are our biggest asset and we want our employees to experience job satisfaction. We have a range of employee benefits we offer nationally across the business:
- We invest in our employee's career growth and development through both internal and company funded external training (Certificate pathway in Laboratory Techniques);
- Coverage by an Enterprise Agreement offering above award conditions to all technician staff;
- Additional Overtime, Penalty Rates, and Living Away from Home Allowance (subject to project undertaking);
- Employee referral program with referral incentives and rewards;
- Access to accommodation options (subject to project undertaking);
- Company Car (subject to project undertaking);
- Opportunities to travel and see more of Australia working in our network of labs;
- Company initiatives such as recognition & reward program, monthly lab events/competitions and health and wellness initiatives (EAP);
- Additional paid parental leave;
- Novated vehicle leasing options.
We believe in equal opportunity
We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive workforce where equity, respect and belonging are valued. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, members of the LGBTQIA+ community, and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. We recognise and value the unique talents, experiences and perspectives that a diverse workforce brings to our business and encourage you to apply.
Next Steps
If this opportunity sparks your interests, please click "Apply" and submit your application via SEEK or on our Careers Page.
No applications will be accepted via email.
